			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Name of the Game"
			icon: {
				id: "mekanismtools:refined_obsidian_pickaxe"
				Count: 1b
				tag: {
					Damage: 0
				}
			}
			x: 6.25d
			y: -1.75d
			shape: "pentagon"
			subtitle: "Well, part of it"
			description: [
				"&7The last two ways you'll be able to find Vulnerabilities is by just... mining and fishing. Simple, but it shows just how much of this whole super megaserver is both held in an iron grip, and held together with duct tape."
				""
				"&7Mining certain ores, mostly ones that break into pieces like Coal or Redstone, give you a chance to find some Code Snippets."
				""
				"&7As for fishing? Self explanatory. Raise up your Fishing Skill from ProjectMMO, and you'll start getting Code Snippets instead of Cod Filets."
			]
			dependencies: ["0F59DB9FD98F0E2E"]
			id: "30F6D2F31395772F"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7A83F82E36155880"
				type: "checkmark"
				title: "Name of the Game"
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "2CD164821D060313"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			icon: {
				id: "minecraft:potion"
				Count: 1b
				tag: {
					Potion: "quark:danger_sight"
				}
			}
			x: 1.25d
			y: -0.5d
			shape: "square"
			subtitle: "or The Rest of the Owl"
			description: [
				"&7Aside from the piratey thing, I'll start up dialogue with the rest of the Researchers here so they can help guide you through the other parts of the FOP Game Server."
				""
				"&7There are lots of mods, with lots of items and machines that the FOP don't really explain to Users. Sure, some have manuals, or guides, but nothing like someone guiding you themselves, yeah? The FOP is more interested in you just sending them the items."
				""
				"&7Now, some of these mods you'll recognize from the previous world, but they may be quite different than you remember. Others will be brand new to you. Either way, the Researchers will start from square one when teaching you."
				""
				"&7And just like before, following the lessons gets you rewards. Money and Blind Boxes. The more we learn, the more we spread the Audobon Worm, the better off we all are."
			]
			dependencies: ["15363C5FC01E875C"]
			id: "132E43CB29BBE90C"
			tasks: [{
				id: "29CE765A6E96998D"
				type: "checkmark"
				title: "The Researchers"
			}]
		}
		{
			icon: "calemiutils:coin_quarter"
			x: 3.25d
			y: -0.5d
			shape: "square"
			subtitle: "Don't Forget the Microtransactions!"
			description: [
				"&7And, of course, we can't forget the DLC the FOP has cut everything into..."
				""
				"&7The basic game, Minecraft, is only slightly gated. You can do most things, aside from Ores, Dimensions, etc, without buying DLC for 'vanilla' minecraft items. Oh, and anything Advent of Ascension? They think limiting Dimension and Ore access is enough."
				""
				"&7Though, I don't think Kowa was able to unlock the highest end Minecraft stuff from DLC. Netherrite tools and armor will still require you to be an appropriate level to equip them."
				""
				"&7As for the DLC? Most mods are grouped with one or two others, but split into the stupid ranking system the FOP came up with."
				""
				"&7Good news? Most mods are only split between Red, Orange, and Yellow ranks. Anything higher rank can match up to high end AoA items, thus the DLC to gate it."
			]
			dependencies: ["132E43CB29BBE90C"]
			id: "3538C7DDF1408271"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7136D17D2E30849A"
				type: "checkmark"
				title: "Multipass?"
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "The Research Division"
			x: 1.25d
			y: 0.75d
			shape: "gear"
			description: [
				"&7So I'm going to unlock the Research and Development section for you now, Bandit."
				""
				"&7Each quest page here will cover one or more mods. Some Researchers or Research Teams may bundle multiple mods together to cover on a single page."
				""
				"&7Keep in mind you'll also need the DLC unlocked to start making items from the appropriate mods. "
				""
				"&7I'll more or less have the Q.U.E.S.T. Tablet sort the Research pages alphabetically to the main mod they cover. If it's a Research Group that covers multiple mods, like say both Pam's and Farmer's Delight... um... You'll figure it out! Research Groups will cover similar mods, really."
			]
			dependencies: ["132E43CB29BBE90C"]
			id: "1D0853ADC7295AEB"
			tasks: [{
				id: "72BCCA0DE755EAC5"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
		}
	]
